  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Public pivots, row spaces, row modules/images, column spaces, and column modules now use bounded pivot metadata plus one bulk selector over canonical ZZ, QQ, GF(2), and small GF(p) storage. Equal-ring exact operations forbid full host export; bases are immutable, preserve degenerate shapes, share pivot caches with echelon forms, and pass generated/dynamic, SageMath differential, lifecycle, sanitizer, and benchmark coverage. Exact pivot storage grows only with rank, and M4RI row selection is a generated declared resource operation.",
    "risks": [
      "pnpm test:portable has an unrelated baseline failure in test/gf2-polynomial-packed-core.cjs: the two packed GF(2) polynomial semantic tests raise OverflowError for a uint64 shift count. The failure reproduces on current main and is assigned outside this lane; 214 of 216 portable tests pass.",
      "The public resource paths are validated on linux-x64 and the M4RI resource surface executes through real Wasm. Native linux-arm64 and macos-arm64 validation remain integration responsibilities.",
      "Cross-ring row_space intentionally materializes original generators. The common equal-ring path remains resource-direct; QQ viewed as a ZZ-module is differentially checked against SageMath."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Obtain an independent semantic and architecture review before integration.",
      "Integrate after the unrelated GF(2) polynomial portable failure is repaired or explicitly baseline-waived.",
